## Exact factorization

Let `Delta_H11,C(gamma)` be the selected affine correction update from
UST.G3CU. Its exact rank is 988. The G3CU rank-revealing rows and columns
select polynomial matrices

```text
U in Z[gamma]^(4426 x 988),
W in Z[gamma]^(988 x 4426),
S in Z[gamma]^(988 x 988).
```

Here `U` consists of the selected columns, `W` of the selected rows and `S`
is their intersection. The reduction of `det(S)` modulo 21,817 is nonzero,
so `S` is invertible over `Q(gamma)`. Since `U` already has the full G3CU
rank, exact linear algebra gives

```text
Delta_H11,C = U S^-1 W,
```

or, without division,

```text
Delta_H11,C det(S) = U adj(S) W.
```

All eighteen coefficient matrices for `U`, `S` and `W` are emitted. A
componentwise split-place solve independently reconstructs every entry of
`Delta_H11,C` with zero mismatch.

## Reduced path equation

For

```text
A(a)=A0+a U S^-1 W,
P=A0^-1 U,
x0=A0^-1 b,
```

the full equation `A(a)x=b` is exactly equivalent to

```text
(S+a W P) z = a W x0,
x = x0-Pz.
```

The varying solve is therefore 988-dimensional. This is an exact selected
factorization, not a numerical low-rank approximation.

